{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Do not say in your heart, when He drives them out.</b> When you see that you will defeat them contrary to the way of the world, and recognize that it is a divine act." "Do not err by saying <b>because of my righteousness HaShem brought me to possess.</b> And that in order that I might possess the land swiftly, He drove them out swiftly on account of my merit." "<b>But because of the wickedness of these nations HaShem dispossesses them before you.</b> Behold, the cause for which He wars against them is their wickedness — not in order that you may possess swiftly."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:58.350022503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}